fb5cd" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the domain of our function is $x\\in [-4,4].$ \n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ does not pass the horizontal line test on the interval $x\\in (-1,1).$ In this case, the horizontal line $y=1$ intersects the graph at more than one point.\n\n![](images/d2/d295d104bd8340a8701327e19103bfa8fd12622f1500c405411d2afd8bd47801.png)\n\n- Among the given options, the largest domain on which the function $f(x)$ is invertible is $x\\in [-4,-1)\\cup [0,4].$ On this domain, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/a7/a74a9a3f1fe52a7c841c763ccffb51faa922fdaec56825ef1000b5becc3534fe.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x\\in [-4,-1)\\cup [0,4].$"] ["question-2c532f18-d5b7-5299-a745-04db386fb5cd" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-3f4d2d26-b1de-54c9-b0f1-b5c8e35847c3" :answer-field/id #uuid "3f4d2d26-b1de-54c9-b0f1-b5c8e35847c3"] ["answer-2b1e68d1-3f22-5cb4-8f92-a0dc46488ea6" :answer/id #uuid "2b1e68d1-3f22-5cb4-8f92-a0dc46488ea6"] ["answer-2b1e68d1-3f22-5cb4-8f92-a0dc46488ea6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2b1e68d1-3f22-5cb4-8f92-a0dc46488ea6" :answer/value "x\\in [-1,4]"] ["answer-7e92042a-79aa-5d53-8df9-c19fc7ee5467" :answer/id #uuid "7e92042a-79aa-5d53-8df9-c19fc7ee5467"] ["answer-7e92042a-79aa-5d53-8df9-c19fc7ee5467" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7e92042a-79aa-5d53-8df9-c19fc7ee5467" :answer/value "x\\in [-4,-1)\\cup [0,4]"] ["answer-b4a0926f-0440-50b7-962c-1887a3857632" :answer/id #uuid "b4a0926f-0440-50b7-962c-1887a3857632"] ["answer-b4a0926f-0440-50b7-962c-1887a3857632" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b4a0926f-0440-50b7-962c-1887a3857632" :answer/value "x\\in [-4,-1]"] ["answer-50b0501e-3889-5168-